<PageTitle>The Singularity Workshop · Live Learning Lab</PageTitle>

<div class="shell">
    <header class="topbar">
        <a class="brand" href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Learning" aria-label="Learning center repository">
            <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Visualize/development/docs/assets/moniker.svg" alt="The Singularity Workshop" />
        </a>
        <nav aria-label="Learning center">
            <a href="#live-lab">Live lab</a>
            <a href="#what-runs">What runs</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Learning">Guides</a>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
        <section class="hero">
            <div class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> Your technology, running in this page</div>
            <h1>Press a tick.<br /><em>Watch the model move.</em></h1>
            <p class="lede">This is a live C# learning lab. Each click runs <strong>FSM_API</strong> in your browser, then the Workshop's GUI adapters turn that real state into a readout and a fresh SVG trace.</p>
            <a class="jump" href="#live-lab">Enter the live lab <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
            <div class="stack" aria-label="Technology running in the browser">
                <span>FSM_API · behavior</span><span>GUI.Core · scene model</span><span>GUI.Blazor · live readout</span><span>GUI.SVG · trace</span>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="live-lab" class="lab-section">
            <div class="section-title">
                <div><div class="eyebrow">01 / Make a prediction</div><h2>Can the value stay inside its range?</h2></div>
                <p>It starts at 0. The FSM moves it by the selected step, reverses at each limit, and never wraps around.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="lab-grid">
                <aside class="controls" aria-label="Oscillator controls">
                    <div class="control-head"><span class="eyebrow">Control the model</span><span class="live-chip"><span class="pulse"></span> Running in browser</span></div>
                    <label for="step-size">Step size <output>@_step.ToString("0.###", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)</output></label>
                    <input id="step-size" type="range" min="1" max="5" step="1" value="@_step.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)" @oninput="OnStepChanged" />
                    <div class="scale"><span>1 · fine</span><span>5 · bold</span></div>
                    <div class="button-row">
                        <button class="primary" @onclick="TickOnce">Tick once <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
                        <button @onclick="TickSix">Run 6 ticks</button>
                        <button @onclick="ResetModel">Reset</button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="prediction"><strong>Before you click:</strong> when the marker reaches 10, what state should the FSM enter next?</div>
                    <p class="owner-note">The buttons call <code>FSM_API.Interaction.Update</code>. The value and state shown here come from the same FSM handle.</p>
                </aside>

                <div class="readout-column">
                    <div class="readout-frame">
                        <div class="frame-label"><span>GUI.Blazor render fragment</span><span>built from a GUI.Core node tree</span></div>
                        @_runtimeSummary
                    </div>
                    <div class="visual-frame">
                        <div class="frame-label"><span>GUI.SVG output</span><span>regenerated after every tick</span></div>
                        @((MarkupString)_traceSvg)
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="trace-panel">
                <div class="trace-title"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / Inspect the evidence</div><h3>Observed state trace</h3></div><span class="trace-count">@_runtime.TickNumber updates</span></div>
                <div class="trace-strip" aria-live="polite" aria-label="FSM_API values and states">
                    @foreach (var sample in _runtime.Samples)
                    {
                        <div class="trace-chip @(sample.Tick == _runtime.TickNumber ? "current" : "")">
                            <small>tick @sample.Tick</small><strong>@sample.Value.ToString("0.###", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)</strong><span>@sample.State</span>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="what-runs" class="what-runs">
            <div><div class="eyebrow">One click, real handoffs</div><h2>Follow the state through your stack.</h2><p>These are live package calls in a .NET WebAssembly app—not a JavaScript model that imitates them.</p></div>
            <div class="handoffs">
                <article><b>1</b><h3>FSM_API</h3><p>The button ticks the bounded oscillator. Its handle supplies the current state after the transition rules run.</p><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.GUI/blob/development/samples/demonstrations/FsmDrivenOscillator/Program.cs">Open the source recipe →</a></article>
                <article><b>2</b><h3>GUI.Core + GUI.Blazor</h3><p>The observed tick, value, and state become a semantic node tree. GUI.Blazor renders that tree into the live page.</p><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.GUI/tree/development/src/Blazor">Explore GUI.Blazor →</a></article>
                <article><b>3</b><h3>GUI.SVG</h3><p>The same observed trace becomes a new SVG scene and is serialized in the browser after each update.</p><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.GUI/tree/development/src/SVG">Explore GUI.SVG →</a></article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="source-note">
            <div class="eyebrow">Try, notice, then read deeper</div>
            <p>With step size 3, the source recipe checks the sequence <code>3 → 6 → 9 → 10 → 7 → 4 → 1 → 0</code>, both states, oversized-step clamping, invalid settings, and the rendered SVG structure. This page runs the same behavior in the browser and plots each value reported by FSM_API.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Learning/blob/main/docs/PROBLEM_TO_PROOF.md">Continue to the problem-to-proof lesson →</a>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.Learning">Learning center</a><span> · </span><a href="https://github.com/TrentBest/TheSingularityWorkshop.FSM_COS/blob/master/DOCUMENTATION_STANDARD.md">FSM_COS documentation standard</a></footer>
</div>

@code {
    private double _step = 3;
    private OscillatorRuntime _runtime = default!;
    private RenderFragment _runtimeSummary = default!;
    private string _traceSvg = "";

    protected override void OnInitialized() => ResetModel();

    private void OnStepChanged(ChangeEventArgs args)
    {
        var text = Convert.ToString(args.Value, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
        if (double.TryParse(text, NumberStyles.Float, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out var step))
        {
            _step = step;
            ResetModel();
        }
    }

    private void TickOnce()
    {
        _runtime.Tick();
        RefreshViews();
    }

    private void TickSix()
    {
        for (var i = 0; i < 6; i++)
            _runtime.Tick();
        RefreshViews();
    }

    private void ResetModel()
    {
        _runtime?.Dispose();
        _runtime = new OscillatorRuntime(_step);
        RefreshViews();
    }

    private void RefreshViews()
    {
        _runtimeSummary = _runtime.BuildRuntimeSummary();
        _traceSvg = _runtime.RenderTraceSvg();
    }

    public void Dispose() => _runtime?.Dispose();
}
